\chapter{Project Mnemosyne: Neuro-Sovereign Simulation Engine}

\section{Overview}

Project Mnemosyne is a neuro-sovereign simulation architecture designed
to model, stabilize, and eradicate neurodegenerative pathology through
multi-scale invariant-governed evolution. Mnemosyne integrates
proteostatic molecular dynamics, cellular metabolic flux, synaptic
network fidelity, and organoid-level orchestration into a unified
simulation engine capable of monotonic pathological decay.

The engine enforces eradication invariants that guarantee:
\begin{itemize}
  \item aggregate clearance exceeds aggregation velocity,
  \item synaptic fidelity remains above critical thresholds,
  \item metabolic stability is preserved under perturbation,
  \item no pathological cascade can self-amplify.
\end{itemize}

\section{Molecular \& Proteostatic Mesh}

The molecular layer models amyloid-$\beta$ and tau aggregation kinetics
under proteostatic constraints. The aggregate concentration evolves as:
\begin{equation}
  \frac{d[\text{Agg}]}{dt}
  =
  k_{\text{nuc}} [\text{monomer}]^2
  +
  k_{\text{elong}} [\text{Agg}]
  -
  k_{\text{clear}} [\text{Agg}],
\end{equation}
where:
\begin{itemize}
  \item $k_{\text{nuc}}$ is nucleation rate,
  \item $k_{\text{elong}}$ is fibril elongation rate,
  \item $k_{\text{clear}}$ is clearance rate.
\end{itemize}

Mnemosyne enforces the proteostatic eradication invariant:
\begin{equation}
  R_{\text{proteostasis}}:
  \quad
  \frac{d[\text{Agg}]}{dt} < 0.
\end{equation}

Conformational dynamics are modeled using coarse-grained neural
representations:
\begin{equation}
  M_{\text{conf}}(t)
  =
  f_{\theta}(M_{\text{conf}}(t-1), S_{\text{proteostasis}}),
\end{equation}
where $f_{\theta}$ is a learned conformational transition operator.

\section{Cellular \& Metabolic Substrate}

The cellular layer models mitochondrial bioenergetics, glucose
utilization, and inflammatory signaling. ATP flux evolves according to:
\begin{equation}
  \frac{d[\text{ATP}]}{dt}
  =
  k_{\text{prod}}
  -
  k_{\text{cons}}
  -
  k_{\text{inflam}} I_{\text{microglia}},
\end{equation}
with microglial activation governed by:
\begin{equation}
  \frac{dI_{\text{microglia}}}{dt}
  =
  k_{\text{stim}}
  -
  k_{\text{resolve}} I_{\text{microglia}}.
\end{equation}

Mnemosyne enforces the metabolic stability invariant:
\begin{equation}
  R_{\text{metabolic}}:
  \quad
  \frac{d[\text{ATP}]}{dt} \ge 0.
\end{equation}

STAT3, SRC, and HSP90AA1 pathways are modeled as coupled ODE systems:
\begin{equation}
  \frac{dP_i}{dt}
  =
  \alpha_i P_i
  -
  \beta_i S_{\text{stress}},
\end{equation}
where $P_i$ represents pathway activation.

\section{Network \& Organoid Orchestration}

The network layer models synaptic fidelity, cerebrovascular flow, and
organoid-level neural dynamics. Synaptic fidelity is defined as:
\begin{equation}
  F_{\text{synapse}}
  =
  1 - \epsilon_{\text{noise}},
\end{equation}
with the eradication invariant:
\begin{equation}
  R_{\text{synaptic}}:
  \quad
  F_{\text{synapse}} > 1 - 10^{-8}.
\end{equation}

Organoid dynamics evolve under:
\begin{equation}
  \frac{d\Psi_{\text{organoid}}}{dt}
  =
  F_{\text{neural}}(\Psi)
  +
  F_{\text{vascular}}(\Psi)
  +
  S_{\text{organoid}},
\end{equation}
where multi-omics integration provides:
\begin{equation}
  \Psi_{\text{multi-omics}}
  =
  \big(
    \Psi_{\text{transcript}},
    \Psi_{\text{proteome}},
    \Psi_{\text{metabolome}}
  \big).
\end{equation}

\section{Eradication Invariants for Alzheimer’s and Dementia}

Mnemosyne enforces a unified eradication invariant stack:
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal{R}_{\text{eradication}}
  =
  R_{\text{proteostasis}}
  \land
  R_{\text{synaptic}}
  \land
  R_{\text{metabolic}}
  \land
  R_{\text{anomaly}}.
\end{equation}

